URL parsing, route synchronization, and fallback navigation for /products/:id and /catalog/:catId on live domains (dokandari.com and dukandari.com) have been updated and verified:
Unified History & Custom Route Event Dispatcher (navigateToStoreRoute):
Replaced legacy window.location.hash mutations and partial history.replaceState calls across all navigation components (Header, Footer, MenuDrawer, CategorySquircleBar, CategoryDetailPage, ProductDetailPage, Mobile Navigation Dock, and homepage cards) with navigateToStoreRoute(...).
Every route change updates window.location.pathname cleanly and dispatches a synchronous 'dokandari:urlchange' event so App.tsx transitions state immediately without relying on hashchange.
Multi-Format URL Parsing (extractUrlProductRoute & extractUrlCatalogRoute):
Supports /products/:id, /product/:id, /p/:id, /item/:id, /shop/:id, /catalog/:catId, /category/:catId, /categories/:catId, /cat/:catId, /collection/:catId, query parameters (?product=, ?id=, ?catalog=, ?category=), decoded %2F paths, and appParams fallback parameters.
Preserves full hyphenated product IDs (e.g., dkd-1776101501645-01) across URL resolution, SSR OpenGraph/Schema.org JSON-LD tags, and Meta/TikTok Pixel events.
Zero-Blank-Page Fallback System:
Product Routes (/products/:id): Synchronously resolves the product on initial render using window.__DOKANDARI_SSR_PRODUCT__, exact/alias matching, or an instant synthesized product fallback while Firestore/API hydration completes in the background—eliminating blank or stuck loading screens on external/mobile browsers.
Catalog Routes (/catalog/:catId): Server-side HTML injection now includes window.__DOKANDARI_SSR_CATALOG__ and OpenGraph metadata for catalog URLs, and CategoryDetailPage automatically falls back to displaying available published catalog items if a newly shared category slug has no exact match yet.
